WEBVTT

00:00:15.780 --> 00:00:17.720
Dad wants us to pick
up where he left off --

00:00:17.720 --> 00:00:19.820
Saving people, hunting things.

00:00:19.820 --> 00:00:20.990
The family business.

00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:24.570
Anybody here?

00:00:25.160 --> 00:00:26.550
Dont move.

00:00:28.490 --> 00:00:29.770
Sam? Dean?

00:00:29.770 --> 00:00:30.910
Mom, you know these guys?

00:00:30.910 --> 00:00:33.110
I think these are
John Winchesters boys.

00:00:33.110 --> 00:00:35.130
Hey, Im Ellen. That's my daughter, Jo.

00:00:35.130 --> 00:00:36.500
You're not gonna hit me again, are you?

00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:38.280
You called our dad, said you could help.

00:00:38.280 --> 00:00:39.030
Help with what?

00:00:39.030 --> 00:00:40.410
The demon, of course.

00:00:40.410 --> 00:00:41.850
How do you know about all this?

00:00:41.850 --> 00:00:43.470
Hey, I just run a saloon.

00:00:43.470 --> 00:00:45.830
Hunters have been known to
pass through now and again --

00:00:45.830 --> 00:00:49.170
Including your dada long time
ago. John was like family once.

00:00:49.170 --> 00:00:51.020
You think dad and
Ellen never had a thing?

00:00:51.020 --> 00:00:52.150
No way.

00:00:52.150 --> 00:00:54.080
Then why didn't he tell us about her?

00:00:55.760 --> 00:00:57.190
How did your mom get into this stuff?

00:00:57.190 --> 00:01:00.420
My dad. He was a hunter. He passed away.

00:01:00.680 --> 00:01:01.280
I could help

00:01:01.280 --> 00:01:04.130
I'm sure you could, but I
think your mother might kill me.

00:01:04.130 --> 00:01:06.060
You're afraid of my mother?

00:01:06.650 --> 00:01:07.700
I think so.

00:01:27.490 --> 00:01:29.940
I checked the fuses. They're fine.

00:01:29.940 --> 00:01:31.690
It's the wiring!

00:01:32.080 --> 00:01:35.550
Look, you promised this place
would be ready when I moved in.

00:01:36.500 --> 00:01:38.890
No! You come up now!

00:01:39.250 --> 00:01:41.090
Please.

00:01:41.600 --> 00:01:43.360
Thank you.

00:01:52.380 --> 00:01:54.350
Gross.

00:02:31.140 --> 00:02:33.080
What the hell?

00:02:57.980 --> 00:03:00.010
Los Angeles, California.

00:03:00.010 --> 00:03:01.590
What's in L.A.?

00:03:01.590 --> 00:03:04.030
A young girl's been
kidnapped by an evil cult.

00:03:04.030 --> 00:03:05.220
Yeah?

00:03:05.660 --> 00:03:07.600
The girl got a name? Katie Holmes.

00:03:10.150 --> 00:03:13.760
That's funny.

00:03:18.140 --> 00:03:20.530
Of course, on the other hand, catfight.

00:03:20.530 --> 00:03:22.470
I am your mother! I don't
have to be reasonable!

00:03:22.470 --> 00:03:24.180
You can't keep me here!

00:03:24.180 --> 00:03:25.400
Don't you bet on that, sweetie!

00:03:25.400 --> 00:03:27.430
Are you gonna chain
me up in the basement?

00:03:27.430 --> 00:03:29.710
You've had worse ideas
than that recently.

00:03:29.710 --> 00:03:31.770
You don't want to stay?
Don't -Go back to school!

00:03:31.770 --> 00:03:34.590
I didn't belong there! I was a
freak with a knife collection!

00:03:34.590 --> 00:03:37.830
Getting yourself killed on some dusty
back road -That's where you belong?

00:03:42.720 --> 00:03:45.190
Guys, bad time. Yes, ma'am.

00:03:45.190 --> 00:03:47.430
We rarely drink before 10:00 anyway.

00:03:47.430 --> 00:03:48.750
Wait.

00:03:49.580 --> 00:03:51.100
I want to know what
they think about this.

00:03:51.100 --> 00:03:53.120
I don't care what they think!

00:03:53.120 --> 00:03:54.580
Are you guys open?

00:03:54.580 --> 00:03:56.100
Yes! No!

00:03:59.930 --> 00:04:02.710
We'll just check out
the Arby's down the road.

00:04:23.170 --> 00:04:24.820
Harvelle's.

00:04:24.820 --> 00:04:26.750
Yeah, preacher.

00:04:26.750 --> 00:04:29.790
Three weeks ago, a young girl
disappears from a Philadelphia apartment.

00:04:32.100 --> 00:04:33.320
Take it. It won't bite.

00:04:33.320 --> 00:04:35.750
No, but your mom might.

00:04:38.690 --> 00:04:42.600
And this girl wasn't the first. Over the
past 80 years,6 women have vanished --

00:04:42.600 --> 00:04:45.140
All from the same
building, all young blondes.

00:04:45.140 --> 00:04:47.730
It only happens every decade or two,
so cops never eyeball the pattern.

00:04:48.510 --> 00:04:51.070
So we're either dealing with
one very old serial killer --

00:04:51.070 --> 00:04:54.030
Who put this together? Ash?

00:04:54.030 --> 00:04:55.710
I did it myself.

00:04:58.760 --> 00:05:01.600
I got to admit, we hit
the road for a lot less.

00:05:01.600 --> 00:05:03.690
Good. If you like the
case so much, you take it.

00:05:04.070 --> 00:05:07.050
Joanna Beth, this
family has lost enough.

00:05:07.980 --> 00:05:10.020
I won't lose you, too.

00:05:12.160 --> 00:05:14.130
I just wont.

00:05:17.400 --> 00:05:18.820
Mother told me

00:05:18.820 --> 00:05:21.020
Yes, she told me

00:05:21.020 --> 00:05:24.280
I'd meet girls like you

00:05:24.280 --> 00:05:26.100
She also told me,

00:05:26.100 --> 00:05:28.090
"Stay away

00:05:28.090 --> 00:05:31.610
You'll never know what you'll catch"

00:05:31.610 --> 00:05:33.480
Mommy's all right,

00:05:33.480 --> 00:05:34.950
Daddys all right,

00:05:34.950 --> 00:05:38.430
They just seem a little weird.

00:05:38.430 --> 00:05:42.010
Surrender, surrender.

00:05:43.280 --> 00:05:45.800
I feel kind of bad, snaking jobs case.

00:05:47.070 --> 00:05:49.810
Well, maybe she put
together a good file,

00:05:50.200 --> 00:05:53.020
But could you see her out here
working one of these things?

00:05:53.020 --> 00:05:54.890
I don't think so.

00:05:56.770 --> 00:05:58.130
You getting anything?

00:05:59.500 --> 00:06:01.130
No, not yet.

00:06:06.300 --> 00:06:07.870
What's that?

00:06:08.210 --> 00:06:09.720
What?

00:06:14.890 --> 00:06:16.850
Holy crap.

00:06:24.200 --> 00:06:26.310
That's ectoplasm.

00:06:26.540 --> 00:06:29.250
Well, Sam, I think I know
what we're dealing with here.

00:06:30.630 --> 00:06:33.020
It's the stay-Puft marshmallow man.

00:06:33.800 --> 00:06:37.630
Dean, Ive only seen
this stuff like twice.

00:06:37.630 --> 00:06:41.270
I mean, to make this stuff, you have
to be one majorly pissed-Off spirit.

00:06:42.290 --> 00:06:45.000
Let's find this badass before
he snags any more girls.

00:06:49.100 --> 00:06:51.440
Yeah, it's a great building.
I fixed it up real nice.

00:06:51.440 --> 00:06:52.830
All the apartments come furnished, too.

00:06:52.830 --> 00:06:56.600
Yeah, I love the
furnishings. It's so spacious,

00:06:56.600 --> 00:07:00.940
And the location is
so convenient for me.

00:07:00.940 --> 00:07:02.590
What the hell are you doing here?

00:07:02.590 --> 00:07:04.450
There you are, honey.

00:07:06.060 --> 00:07:08.460
This is my boyfriend,
Dean, and his buddy Sam.

00:07:08.460 --> 00:07:11.230
Good to meet you. Quite
a gal you got here.

00:07:11.230 --> 00:07:13.140
Yeah, she's a pistol!

00:07:13.310 --> 00:07:15.840
So, did you already
check out the apartment?

00:07:17.800 --> 00:07:19.480
The one for rent.

00:07:19.480 --> 00:07:22.770
Yeah. Yes. Loved it. Great flow.

00:07:22.770 --> 00:07:24.440
How'd you get in? It was open.

00:07:25.550 --> 00:07:28.190
Now, Ed, when did the
last tenant move out?

00:07:28.710 --> 00:07:31.390
Uh, about a month ago. Cut and run, too.

00:07:31.390 --> 00:07:32.400
Stiffed me for the rent.

00:07:32.400 --> 00:07:35.170
Well, her loss, our gain,

00:07:35.170 --> 00:07:37.510
'Cause if Dean loves it,
it's good enough for me.

00:07:37.510 --> 00:07:39.460
Oh, sweetie.

00:07:40.120 --> 00:07:41.810
We'll take it.

00:07:44.450 --> 00:07:45.750
Okay.

00:07:49.120 --> 00:07:50.540
I'll flip you for the sofa.

00:07:50.540 --> 00:07:51.900
Does your mother even know youre here?

00:07:51.900 --> 00:07:53.110
I told her I was going to Vegas.

00:07:53.110 --> 00:07:54.200
You think shes gonna buy that?

00:07:54.200 --> 00:07:55.080
I'm not an idiot.

00:07:55.080 --> 00:07:58.010
I got Ash to lay a credit-Card
trail all the way to the casinos.

00:07:58.790 --> 00:08:02.410
You shouldn't lie to your mom.
You shouldn't be here, either.

00:08:04.450 --> 00:08:07.460
Well, I am, so untwist your
boxers and deal with it.

00:08:07.460 --> 00:08:09.400
Where'd you get all
that money from, anyways?

00:08:09.400 --> 00:08:10.400
Working at the roadhouse.

00:08:10.400 --> 00:08:11.640
Hunters don't tip that well.

00:08:11.640 --> 00:08:13.640
They aren't that good at poker, either.

00:08:20.180 --> 00:08:21.920
Yeah? Is she with you?

00:08:23.000 --> 00:08:24.110
Oh, hi, Ellen.

00:08:24.110 --> 00:08:26.750
She left a note shes in Vegas.
I don't believe it for a second.

00:08:29.740 --> 00:08:31.340
Dean? I haven't seen her.

00:08:31.340 --> 00:08:33.600
You sure about that? Yeah, Im sure.

00:08:33.600 --> 00:08:36.730
Well, please, if she shows up, you'll
drag her butt back here, won't you?

00:08:36.730 --> 00:08:38.840
Absolutely. Okay. Thanks, hon.

00:08:43.530 --> 00:08:45.820
This place was built in 1924.

00:08:45.820 --> 00:08:49.180
It was originally a warehouse, converted
into apartments a few months ago.

00:08:50.090 --> 00:08:52.510
Yeah? What was here before 1924?

00:08:52.510 --> 00:08:53.890
Nothing. An empty field.

00:08:53.890 --> 00:08:55.770
So the most
likely scenario --

00:08:55.770 --> 00:08:59.040
Someone died bloody in the building,
and now he's back and raising hell.

00:09:00.510 --> 00:09:02.050
I already checked.

00:09:02.050 --> 00:09:04.750
In the past 82 years,
zero violent deaths,

00:09:04.750 --> 00:09:07.080
Unless you count a janitor
who slipped on a wet floor.

00:09:07.780 --> 00:09:09.910
Would you sit down, please?

00:09:13.010 --> 00:09:15.790
So, have you checked the police
reports, county death records?

00:09:15.790 --> 00:09:19.290
Obituaries, mortuary reports,
and seven other sources.

00:09:19.290 --> 00:09:20.360
I know what I'm doing.

00:09:20.360 --> 00:09:22.540
I think the jury's
still out on that one.

00:09:24.790 --> 00:09:27.070
Would you put the knife down?

00:09:27.450 --> 00:09:30.710
Okay. So, uh, its something else, then.

00:09:30.710 --> 00:09:33.350
Maybe some kind of cursed object
that brought a spirit with it.

00:09:33.350 --> 00:09:36.180
We got to scan the whole
building. Right. So, you and me --

00:09:36.180 --> 00:09:39.860
Well take the top two floors.

00:09:39.860 --> 00:09:42.080
We'd move faster if we split up.

00:09:42.080 --> 00:09:43.980
Oh, this isn't negotiable.

00:09:45.740 --> 00:09:47.980
So, are you gonna buy me dinner?

00:09:48.550 --> 00:09:50.230
What are you talking about?

00:09:50.600 --> 00:09:54.030
It's just if you're gonna ride me this
close, it's only decent you buy me dinner.

00:09:54.410 --> 00:09:55.980
Oh, that's hilarious.

00:09:55.980 --> 00:09:57.520
Its bad enough I lied to your mom,

00:09:57.520 --> 00:09:59.480
But if you think I'm letting
you out of my sight --

00:09:59.480 --> 00:10:01.960
I don't know if you noticed, but
you're kind of the spirit's type.

00:10:02.340 --> 00:10:03.680
Exactly.

00:10:04.580 --> 00:10:05.900
You want to be bait?

00:10:05.900 --> 00:10:07.740
The quickest way to draw
it out, and you know it.

00:10:08.340 --> 00:10:09.890
What? I'm so regretting this.

00:10:10.580 --> 00:10:13.010
I've had it up to herewith your crap.

00:10:13.790 --> 00:10:14.700
Excuse me?

00:10:14.700 --> 00:10:16.400
Your chauvinist crap.

00:10:16.400 --> 00:10:18.070
You think women cant do the job.

00:10:18.070 --> 00:10:21.620
Sweetheart, this ain't gender
studies. Women can do the job fine.

00:10:21.620 --> 00:10:24.000
Amateurs cant. You got no experience.

00:10:24.000 --> 00:10:28.620
What you do have is a bunch of half-Baked romantic
notions that some barfly has put in your head.

00:10:28.620 --> 00:10:30.260
And now you sound like my mother.

00:10:30.260 --> 00:10:32.470
Oh, and that's a bad thing?
Because let me tell you --

00:10:32.470 --> 00:10:34.410
What?

00:10:36.720 --> 00:10:38.340
Forget it.

00:10:38.340 --> 00:10:39.790
No, you started this.

00:10:39.790 --> 00:10:43.510
Jo, you got options. No one in
their right mind chooses this life.

00:10:43.510 --> 00:10:46.880
My dad started me in this when I was so
young. I wish I could do something else.

00:10:46.880 --> 00:10:48.110
You love the job.

00:10:48.110 --> 00:10:49.550
Yeah, but Im a little twisted.

00:10:49.550 --> 00:10:52.190
You don't think Im
a little twisted, too?

00:10:53.840 --> 00:10:56.130
Jo, you got a mother
that worries about you,

00:10:56.130 --> 00:10:59.460
Who wants something more for
you. Those are good things.

00:11:00.120 --> 00:11:02.840
You don't throw things like that away.

00:11:03.210 --> 00:11:05.560
They might be hard to find later.

00:11:42.920 --> 00:11:44.290
What?

00:11:47.080 --> 00:11:48.750
I'm not sure.

00:11:51.430 --> 00:11:52.910
Do you smell that?

00:11:54.460 --> 00:11:56.360
What is it, a gas leak?

00:11:56.360 --> 00:11:58.720
No. Its something else.

00:12:00.360 --> 00:12:04.190
I know it. I just can't
put my finger on it.

00:12:11.180 --> 00:12:13.520
Mazel Tov. You just
found your first spirit.

00:12:14.740 --> 00:12:16.760
It's inside the vent.

00:12:23.390 --> 00:12:24.970
Here.

00:12:44.820 --> 00:12:46.460
There's something in there. Here.

00:13:09.130 --> 00:13:11.440
Someone's keeping souvenirs.

00:14:03.570 --> 00:14:05.830
This building --
I swear to god.

00:14:30.030 --> 00:14:31.910
I'm so out of here.

00:15:14.300 --> 00:15:15.980
Morning, princess.

00:15:16.770 --> 00:15:19.040
Where's Sam? Went to get coffee.

00:15:24.030 --> 00:15:25.730
My back.

00:15:28.220 --> 00:15:31.110
How'd you sleep on that big, soft bed?

00:15:31.110 --> 00:15:32.760
I didnt.

00:15:32.760 --> 00:15:35.300
I've just been going over everything.

00:15:48.220 --> 00:15:49.830
Here.

00:15:49.830 --> 00:15:51.160
What's this for?

00:15:51.160 --> 00:15:54.570
It'll work a hell of a lot better than that
little pig stick you've been twirling around.

00:16:07.830 --> 00:16:10.460
William Anthony Harvelle.

00:16:12.880 --> 00:16:15.280
I'm sorry. My mistake.

00:16:26.020 --> 00:16:28.160
What do
you --

00:16:28.160 --> 00:16:30.150
What do you remember about your dad?

00:16:30.890 --> 00:16:33.850
What's the first thing
that pops into your head?

00:16:38.380 --> 00:16:40.660
Come on. Tell me.

00:16:48.490 --> 00:16:51.070
I was 6 or 7...

00:16:52.150 --> 00:16:54.320
And, uh...

00:16:54.860 --> 00:16:57.290
He took me shooting for the first time.

00:16:57.290 --> 00:17:00.340
Bottles on a fence
--That kind of thing.

00:17:01.650 --> 00:17:03.790
I bull's-Eyed every one of them.

00:17:05.750 --> 00:17:09.030
And he would smile, like...

00:17:12.020 --> 00:17:13.740
I dont know.

00:17:15.950 --> 00:17:17.960
He must have been proud.

00:17:20.600 --> 00:17:22.890
What about your dad?

00:17:24.920 --> 00:17:27.760
I was still in pigtails
when my dad died, but...

00:17:28.680 --> 00:17:31.640
I remember him coming home from a hunt.

00:17:32.120 --> 00:17:34.510
He'd burst through
that door like --

00:17:34.710 --> 00:17:37.230
Like Steve McQueen or something.

00:17:38.100 --> 00:17:40.410
And he'd sweep me up in his arms,

00:17:40.780 --> 00:17:43.350
And I'd breathe in that
old leather jacket of his.

00:17:44.840 --> 00:17:48.000
And my mom --Who
was sour and pissed

00:17:48.000 --> 00:17:51.050
From the minute he left
She started smiling again.

00:17:52.090 --> 00:17:53.950
And we were...

00:17:55.210 --> 00:17:57.090
We were a family.

00:18:03.490 --> 00:18:06.090
You want to know why
I want to do the job?

00:18:06.930 --> 00:18:09.120
For him.

00:18:09.700 --> 00:18:12.210
It's my way of being close to him.

00:18:13.360 --> 00:18:15.490
Now, tell me, what's wrong with that?

00:18:17.090 --> 00:18:18.860
Nothing.

00:18:25.260 --> 00:18:27.590
Where's the coffee?
There are cops outside.

00:18:28.570 --> 00:18:30.690
Another girl disappeared.

00:18:38.750 --> 00:18:41.300
Theresa Ellis
--Apartment 2-F.

00:18:41.300 --> 00:18:43.530
Her boyfriend reported
her missing around dawn.

00:18:43.530 --> 00:18:45.070
And her apartment?

00:18:45.070 --> 00:18:48.000
Cracks all over the
plaster --Walls, ceiling.

00:18:48.000 --> 00:18:49.510
There's ectoplasm, too.

00:18:49.510 --> 00:18:52.710
Between that and that tuft of hair, I'd
say the suckers coming from the walls.

00:18:52.710 --> 00:18:55.970
But who is it? The building's
history's totally clean.

00:18:58.370 --> 00:19:00.590
Maybe we're looking in the wrong place.

00:19:00.590 --> 00:19:03.170
What do you mean? Check this out.

00:19:06.830 --> 00:19:07.980
An empty field?

00:19:07.980 --> 00:19:11.770
It's where this building was built.
Take a look at the one next door.

00:19:13.130 --> 00:19:15.550
The windows.

00:19:17.490 --> 00:19:18.520
Bars.

00:19:18.520 --> 00:19:20.430
We're next door to a prison?

00:19:20.430 --> 00:19:21.680
Thanks, Ash.

00:19:21.680 --> 00:19:23.710
Oh, and if you breathe a
word of this to my mom --

00:19:23.710 --> 00:19:27.760
Thats right. I will. With pliers.

00:19:28.420 --> 00:19:30.750
Okay. Moyamensing
prison --

00:19:30.750 --> 00:19:34.530
Built in 1835, torn down
in 1963. And get this --

00:19:34.530 --> 00:19:38.380
They used to execute people by hanging
them in the empty field next door.

00:19:39.630 --> 00:19:42.890
Well, then, we need a list of
all the people executed there.

00:19:42.890 --> 00:19:44.860
Ash is already on it.

00:19:51.240 --> 00:19:53.930
157 names?

00:19:54.370 --> 00:19:56.410
We got to narrow that down. Yeah.

00:19:56.410 --> 00:19:59.090
Or else we're gonna be digging
up a hell of a lot of stiffs.

00:20:06.230 --> 00:20:08.200
Herman Webster Mudgett?

00:20:09.830 --> 00:20:11.580
Yeah?

00:20:12.550 --> 00:20:15.560
Wasn't that H.H. Holmes' real name?

00:20:17.070 --> 00:20:19.480
You got to be kidding me.

00:20:25.860 --> 00:20:29.240
Holmes was executed at
Moyamensing may 7,1896.

00:20:29.330 --> 00:20:31.490
H.H. Holmes himself.

00:20:31.900 --> 00:20:33.640
Come on. I mean, what are the odds?

00:20:33.640 --> 00:20:35.470
Who is this guy?

00:20:35.470 --> 00:20:38.800
The term "multi-Murderer" --
They coined it to describe Holmes.

00:20:38.800 --> 00:20:42.100
He was Americas first serial killer before
anybody knew what a serial killer was.

00:20:42.100 --> 00:20:45.620
He confessed to 27 murders, but
some put the death toll at over 100.

00:20:45.620 --> 00:20:49.220
And his victim flavor of
choice -Pretty, petite blondes.

00:20:49.620 --> 00:20:52.620
He, uh, used chloroform to kill them,

00:20:53.550 --> 00:20:55.920
Which is what I smelled
in the hallway last night.

00:20:58.050 --> 00:20:59.780
At his place, cops found human remains,

00:20:59.780 --> 00:21:03.400
Bone fragments, and long
locks of bloody blond hair.

00:21:03.400 --> 00:21:05.520
Boy, he sure knew how to pick them.

00:21:05.520 --> 00:21:08.190
We just find the bones, salt
them, and burn them, right?

00:21:08.190 --> 00:21:09.520
It's not that easy.

00:21:09.520 --> 00:21:11.800
His body is buried in town,

00:21:11.800 --> 00:21:14.500
But it's encased in a
couple tons of concrete.

00:21:14.500 --> 00:21:16.210
What? Why?

00:21:16.210 --> 00:21:19.490
The story goes that he didn't
want anybody mutilating his corpse

00:21:19.490 --> 00:21:22.210
'Cause, you know, it's
what he used to do.

00:21:22.210 --> 00:21:24.120
You know something?

00:21:26.240 --> 00:21:28.100
We might have an even
bigger problem than that.

00:21:28.100 --> 00:21:30.080
How does this get bigger?

00:21:30.780 --> 00:21:33.040
Holmes built an apartment
building in Chicago.

00:21:33.040 --> 00:21:36.340
They called it the murder castle.
The whole place was a death factory.

00:21:36.340 --> 00:21:39.500
They had trapdoors, acid
vats, quicklime pits.

00:21:39.500 --> 00:21:42.110
He built these secret chambers...

00:21:42.110 --> 00:21:44.020
Inside the walls.

00:21:44.020 --> 00:21:46.230
He'd lock his victims in,
keep them alive for days.

00:21:46.230 --> 00:21:48.030
Some, he'd suffocate.

00:21:48.030 --> 00:21:50.160
Others, he'd let starve to death.

00:21:50.160 --> 00:21:54.200
So Theresa could still be alive.
She could be inside these walls.

00:21:54.200 --> 00:21:56.660
We need sledgehammers, crowbars.
We got to smash these walls

00:21:56.660 --> 00:21:58.920
Anywhere thick enough to hide a girl.

00:22:13.610 --> 00:22:17.000
Okay. Call us after you
check the southeast wall.

00:22:18.110 --> 00:22:20.930
Sam's almost done with the first floor.

00:22:21.400 --> 00:22:23.630
He hasn't found jack squat, either.

00:22:30.410 --> 00:22:31.650
What is it?

00:22:31.650 --> 00:22:34.200
It's too narrow. We
can't go any further.

00:22:34.200 --> 00:22:35.900
Let me see. -
What are you --

00:22:39.410 --> 00:22:41.310
I should have cleaned the pipes. What?

00:22:41.310 --> 00:22:43.760
I wish the pipes were clean.

00:22:44.290 --> 00:22:45.730
Shut up!

00:22:45.730 --> 00:22:47.250
I can fit in there.

00:22:47.640 --> 00:22:49.000
You're not going in thereby yourself.

00:22:49.000 --> 00:22:50.610
You got a better idea?

00:22:50.610 --> 00:22:52.040
The
--

00:23:15.280 --> 00:23:17.500
Where are you? By the north wall.

00:23:37.510 --> 00:23:40.440
I'm heading down some kind of air duct.

00:23:40.440 --> 00:23:42.270
No, no, no, no. Stay up here.

00:23:42.270 --> 00:23:44.400
We got to find this girl, don't we?

00:23:45.040 --> 00:23:46.470
I'm okay.

00:23:46.470 --> 00:23:48.410
All right. Im heading to you.

00:24:22.890 --> 00:24:24.210
Oh, god.

00:24:24.840 --> 00:24:26.410
What is it?

00:24:27.310 --> 00:24:29.790
Jo? Jo?!

00:24:38.020 --> 00:24:39.420
Jo!

00:25:01.370 --> 00:25:03.140
Jo?!

00:25:05.510 --> 00:25:07.260
Jo!

00:25:16.500 --> 00:25:18.620
He's got Jo. What? Howd that happen?

00:25:18.620 --> 00:25:20.690
I wasn't with her. I
left her alone. Damn it!

00:25:20.690 --> 00:25:23.490
Look, we'll find her. Where? Inside
the walls. We were inside the walls.

00:25:23.490 --> 00:25:26.830
None of the other girls are
there. She won't be, either.

00:25:27.840 --> 00:25:30.650
Look, take a beat and think about
this. Maybe we got Holmes' M.O. Wrong.

00:25:30.650 --> 00:25:32.670
Well, we better friggin' think fast.

00:25:36.210 --> 00:25:37.100
Yeah?

00:25:37.100 --> 00:25:39.070
You lied to me. Shes there.

00:25:39.070 --> 00:25:41.380
Ellen. Ash told me everything.

00:25:41.380 --> 00:25:43.400
The man's a genius, but
he folds like a cheap suit.

00:25:43.400 --> 00:25:44.880
You put my damn daughter on the phone.

00:25:44.880 --> 00:25:48.300
She's gonna have to call you back. She's,
uh, taking care of feminine business.

00:25:48.300 --> 00:25:50.520
Yeah, right. Where is she?

00:25:50.990 --> 00:25:52.980
Where is she?!

00:25:53.420 --> 00:25:54.580
Look, we'll get her back.

00:25:54.580 --> 00:25:57.020
Get her back? Back from what?

00:25:57.020 --> 00:25:58.690
The spirit we're
hunting --It took her.

00:25:58.690 --> 00:25:59.410
Oh, my god.

00:25:59.410 --> 00:26:00.930
She'll be okay. I promise. You promise?

00:26:00.930 --> 00:26:04.800
That is not the first time Ive
heard that from a Winchester.

00:26:05.050 --> 00:26:05.920
What?

00:26:05.920 --> 00:26:07.840
If anything
happens to her --

00:26:07.840 --> 00:26:09.370
It wont. I won't let it.

00:26:09.370 --> 00:26:11.180
Ellen, Im sorry. I really am.

00:26:11.180 --> 00:26:13.870
I'm taking the first flight out.
I'll be there in a few hours.

00:26:16.330 --> 00:26:18.620
Damn it!

00:26:18.620 --> 00:26:21.680
Don't beat yourself up, Dean.
There's nothing you could have done.

00:26:21.680 --> 00:26:23.190
Tell me you got something.

00:26:23.190 --> 00:26:24.460
Uh, maybe.

00:26:25.900 --> 00:26:27.180
Look.

00:26:27.180 --> 00:26:28.950
If you look at the layout
of the Holmes murder castle,

00:26:28.950 --> 00:26:31.220
Theres other torture chambers
inside the walls, right?

00:26:31.640 --> 00:26:33.630
But there's one we
havent considered yet --

00:26:33.630 --> 00:26:34.990
The one in his basement.

00:26:34.990 --> 00:26:36.050
This building doesn't have a basement.

00:26:36.050 --> 00:26:38.710
You're right. It doesnt.
But I just noticed this.

00:26:38.800 --> 00:26:40.320
Beneath the foundation,

00:26:40.320 --> 00:26:42.530
It looks like part of an old sewer
system. It hasn't been used for --

00:26:42.530 --> 00:26:43.980
Lets go.

00:27:54.580 --> 00:27:55.910
Hello?

00:28:05.920 --> 00:28:07.900
Is -Is anybody there?

00:28:08.530 --> 00:28:10.910
Your name's Theresa?

00:28:12.320 --> 00:28:14.000
Yes.

00:28:14.000 --> 00:28:16.850
This won't make you feel better, but...

00:28:17.420 --> 00:28:19.630
I'm here to rescue you.

00:28:20.260 --> 00:28:23.420
Oh, god. He's out there.
He's gonna kill us!

00:28:23.420 --> 00:28:25.490
No, he won't!

00:28:25.490 --> 00:28:27.760
We're getting out.

00:28:27.760 --> 00:28:30.470
My friends are looking for us.

00:28:31.360 --> 00:28:33.220
Oh, god, it's him!

00:28:33.220 --> 00:28:35.530
Shh! Just be quiet!

00:29:37.140 --> 00:29:38.760
Here.

00:30:05.820 --> 00:30:07.490
Got it? Yeah.

00:31:09.550 --> 00:31:11.190
You're so pretty.

00:31:15.310 --> 00:31:17.220
So beautiful.

00:31:17.220 --> 00:31:19.240
Go to hell!

00:31:52.180 --> 00:31:53.800
How do you like that?!

00:31:53.800 --> 00:31:56.790
Pure iron, you
creepy-Ass son of a bitch!

00:33:00.270 --> 00:33:02.100
Is he gone?

00:33:03.170 --> 00:33:05.170
I don't
know. I --

00:33:23.030 --> 00:33:24.670
Hey!

00:33:25.720 --> 00:33:27.070
No!

00:33:28.630 --> 00:33:29.870
Jo!

00:33:30.290 --> 00:33:32.040
I'm here!

00:33:56.460 --> 00:33:58.380
Hey. I'm gonna get you
out of here, all right?

00:33:58.910 --> 00:34:00.560
Sam!

00:34:02.870 --> 00:34:04.570
Hang on.

00:34:07.440 --> 00:34:10.050
You all right? I've been better.

00:34:10.600 --> 00:34:13.200
Let's get the hell out of
here before he comes back.

00:34:13.200 --> 00:34:16.240
Actually, I don't think
you're leaving here just yet.

00:34:16.240 --> 00:34:16.920
What?

00:34:16.920 --> 00:34:19.500
Remember when I said you
being bait was a bad plan?

00:34:19.500 --> 00:34:21.650
Now it's kind of the only one we got.

00:35:36.600 --> 00:35:37.920
Now!

00:35:57.520 --> 00:36:01.450
Scream all you want! There's no
way you're stepping over that salt!

00:36:12.000 --> 00:36:13.660
So...

00:36:13.660 --> 00:36:16.370
Is this job as glamorous
as you thought it would be?

00:36:17.390 --> 00:36:19.780
Well, except for all the
peeYour-Pants terror, yeah.

00:36:20.440 --> 00:36:23.200
But that Theresa girl's gonna
live a life 'cause of us.

00:36:23.570 --> 00:36:24.860
It's worth it, isn't it?

00:36:24.860 --> 00:36:26.290
Yeah.

00:36:26.290 --> 00:36:27.740
Yeah, it is.

00:36:27.740 --> 00:36:29.680
Hey, what if somebody
finds that sewer done there

00:36:29.680 --> 00:36:31.580
Or a storm washes the salt away?

00:36:31.580 --> 00:36:34.900
Both very fine points, which
is why we're waiting here.

00:36:34.900 --> 00:36:36.410
For what?

00:36:42.830 --> 00:36:44.470
For that.

00:37:05.710 --> 00:37:07.650
You ripped off a cement truck?

00:37:07.650 --> 00:37:09.160
I'll give it back.

00:37:24.600 --> 00:37:27.740
Well, that ought to keep him
down there till hell freezes over.

00:38:01.340 --> 00:38:04.840
Well, you -You really weren't
kidding about flying out, were you?

00:38:18.170 --> 00:38:20.240
How about we listen to some music?

00:38:20.980 --> 00:38:24.030
You're as cold as ice.

00:38:34.640 --> 00:38:36.850
This is gonna be a long drive.

00:38:44.540 --> 00:38:46.300
Ellen...

00:38:46.300 --> 00:38:50.160
It was my fault. Okay? I
lied to you, and I'm sorry.

00:38:50.160 --> 00:38:52.420
But Jo did good out there. I
think her dad would be proud.

00:38:52.420 --> 00:38:55.100
Don't you dare
say that --Not you.

00:38:55.100 --> 00:38:57.730
I need a moment with
my daughter -Alone.

00:39:06.770 --> 00:39:08.320
You're angry. I understand.

00:39:08.320 --> 00:39:10.210
Angry doesn't beg into touch it!

00:39:10.210 --> 00:39:12.860
Let's just think about
this. Everything's okay.

00:39:12.860 --> 00:39:14.350
I'm alive.

00:39:14.350 --> 00:39:15.890
Not after Im through with you!

00:39:15.890 --> 00:39:17.320
Is this about me hunting
or something else?

00:39:17.320 --> 00:39:18.940
You let those boys use you as bait.

00:39:18.940 --> 00:39:20.710
They were backing me up the whole time.

00:39:20.710 --> 00:39:22.620
That is why you do not have
the sense to do this job.

00:39:22.620 --> 00:39:24.360
You're trusting your life to
them. What are you talking about?

00:39:24.360 --> 00:39:26.720
Like father, like son.
That is what Im talking...

00:39:32.020 --> 00:39:33.770
John?

00:39:36.300 --> 00:39:38.500
I thought you and John were friends.

00:39:38.500 --> 00:39:40.620
Yeah, we were. I'm
sorry. I didn't mean --

00:39:40.620 --> 00:39:42.030
Mom...

00:39:44.720 --> 00:39:47.300
What aren't you telling me?

00:40:03.510 --> 00:40:05.370
That bad, huh? Not right now.

00:40:06.970 --> 00:40:08.640
What happened? Hey, talk to me.

00:40:08.640 --> 00:40:10.310
Get off me!

00:40:10.890 --> 00:40:12.690
Sorry. Ill see you around.

00:40:12.690 --> 00:40:14.900
Dean...

00:40:18.730 --> 00:40:21.830
It turns out my dad had a
partner on his last hunt.

00:40:21.830 --> 00:40:24.110
Funny, he usually worked
alone. This guy did, too.

00:40:24.110 --> 00:40:28.110
But I guess my father
figured he could trust him.

00:40:28.870 --> 00:40:32.560
A mistake. The guy screwed
up, got my dad killed.

00:40:32.560 --> 00:40:34.920
What does this have --
It was your father, Dean.

00:40:35.940 --> 00:40:37.480
What?

00:40:37.480 --> 00:40:41.090
Why do you think John never came
back, never told you about us?

00:40:41.090 --> 00:40:43.990
'Cause he couldn't look my mom
in the eye after that -That's why.

00:40:44.430 --> 00:40:46.130
Jo --
Just --

00:40:46.130 --> 00:40:48.360
Just get out of here.

00:40:49.200 --> 00:40:51.040
Please, just leave.



00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:17.000
